---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Alabama Mountain Property | The Bluffs — Overlooking Weiss Lake"
  description="The Bluffs sits on a mountain peninsula extending into Weiss Lake in the Appalachian foothills of Northeast Alabama — comparable to the mountains of North Georgia, North Carolina, and Tennessee."
  image="/assets/images/pages/mountain-lake.jpg"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="page-hero">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/pages/mountain-lake.jpg"
      alt="Autumn lake view from an elevated overlook at The Bluffs on Weiss Lake"
      width="1920"
      height="800"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
    <div class="page-hero-overlay">
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">Alabama Mountain Property at the Bluffs</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- BLOCK 1: Appalachian Foothills -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split-block">
        <div class="split-text prose">
          <h2>The Appalachian Foothills of Northeast Alabama</h2>
          <p>
            Most people think of Georgia, North Carolina, or Tennessee when they think of
            Appalachian mountain country — but Northeast Alabama is every bit as beautiful,
            and considerably less crowded. The ridge lines, hardwood forests, and cool
            seasons of Cherokee County rival anything you'll find across the state lines,
            at a fraction of the price.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Bluffs sits in this underappreciated landscape: elevated, forested, and
            perched above one of the best bass-fishing lakes in the Southeast. It is a place
            that feels remote but isn't — it simply hasn't been discovered yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-image">
          <img
            src="/assets/images/pages/mountain-sunset.jpg"
            alt="Panoramic sunset over the mountain ridgeline near Weiss Lake"
            width="800"
            height="600"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin: 0 auto;" />

  <!-- BLOCK 2: Geology / Building -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split-block reverse">
        <div class="split-text prose">
          <h2>The Coosa Valley — A Practical Place to Build</h2>
          <p>
            The Appalachian Valley, also known as the Coosa Valley in Alabama, sits atop a
            limestone belt — a geology that produces flat, easy-to-build ridge tops even within
            otherwise dramatic mountain terrain. This means that building a home at The Bluffs
            is more straightforward than it might appear from the landscape. Homesites are
            graded to make construction practical without sacrificing the elevation and views
            that make them special.
          </p>
          <p>
            The result is a community where dramatic scenery and buildable lots coexist —
            a combination that's genuinely rare.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="split-image">
          <img
            src="/assets/images/pages/mountain-aerial.jpg"
            alt="Aerial satellite view of the Weiss Lake peninsula where The Bluffs is located"
            width="800"
            height="600"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin: 0 auto;" />

  <!-- BLOCK 3: The Peninsula -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split-block">
        <div class="split-text prose">
          <h2>A Mountain Finger in Weiss Lake</h2>
          <p>
            The Bluffs occupies a mountain peninsula — imagine a mountain finger poking out
            into the 30,000-acre expanse of Weiss Lake. This geography means that most
            homesites are surrounded by water on three sides, creating an extraordinary
            sense of seclusion and panoramic views that a typical lakefront lot simply
            cannot offer.
          </p>
          <p>
            Weiss Lake itself stretches 52 miles and is widely regarded as the crappie
            fishing capital of the world, with outstanding bass fishing as well.
            The surrounding Piedmont Mountain Range frames the horizon on every clear day.
          </p>
          <p>
            Located approximately 90 miles from Atlanta, 90 miles from Birmingham, and
            80 miles from Chattanooga, The Bluffs is genuinely accessible from any of the
            ABC Triangle metros — yet it feels like a world apart.
          </p>
          <a href="/homesites" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">View Available Homesites</a>
        </div>
        <div class="split-image">
          <img
            src="/assets/images/pages/mountain-lake.jpg"
            alt="Fall colors along the lake overlook at The Bluffs"
            width="800"
            height="600"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .split-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .split-block.reverse .split-text {
    order: 2;
  }

  .split-block.reverse .split-image {
    order: 1;
  }

  .split-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 400px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .split-text h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .split-text.prose p {
    color: var(--color-charcoal-mid);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .split-block {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }

    .split-block.reverse .split-text,
    .split-block.reverse .split-image {
      order: unset;
    }

    .split-image img {
      height: 260px;
    }
  }
</style>
